  "slug": "coding-rnas-generates-6c5b",
  "summary": "New portals and databases harmonize spatial and single-cell datasets at scale, while workflows and toolkits standardize cohort-level analysis and provenance.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is infrastructure that consolidates heterogeneous spatial and single-cell data and standardizes access. The HuBMAP Data Portal hosts 9,316 public datasets from healthy human tissues, and STRAND harmonizes 35 subcellular-resolution spatial transcriptomics datasets (~4.9 billion transcript coordinates). SpaceBlocks provides a Snakemake workflow for reproducible, expert-supervised cohort-level analysis, and Pycea with TreeData integrates lineage trees into scverse/Scanpy. TRACE emphasizes traceable curation, shown on a harmonised single-cell glaucoma resource. PathoEvo, CircaVal and R-loopBase v2.0 apply database approaches to disease progression, circadian regulation and R-loops, and are less specifically spatial. The contribution is integration, provenance and access rather than new inference methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-05"
}
